Negative control for the FE-3113 executed matrix (`AC1` · `AC3`).

A module arms the recorded paths belonging to the SUBJECT its own `.feature`
declares — the recordings supply the paths, the feature decides which are the
module's own. The mutant sends the whole question back to the recordings: every
path the capture run touched arms, chrome included. Nothing under-reaches, so
every module still arms all of its own endpoints and every preset still answers;
what is added is the country lookup and the brand-config read a capture run
needed to populate a form, where forcing `loading` hangs the app chrome for the
tab's life.

What must go red is OVER-reach and the source it is read from. An assertion that
each subject path arms passes the mutant untouched, and so does one that only
counts routes. Require a recorded path the module does NOT arm, and hand one
module's recordings another module's feature — a recordings-only derivation
cannot give a different answer to that, and the mutant gives the same answer to
an empty feature as to the module's own.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the all-modules matrix — the subject is narrower than the capture run, and
takes its subject from the FEATURE.

